From c90db29c631a2603c4baa3e443d646c1d54aea65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:40:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] speculative + qwen35: greedy MTP drafts as one unrolled
 draft-chain graph

draft-mtp with greedy drafting (p_min 0, not probabilistic), one MTP head and a reduced draft vocabulary
(--spec-draft-vocab) now decodes the n_max draft tokens with a single llama_process: the MTP graph
unrolls n_max single-token passes, each taking the argmax over the draft head of the previous pass
(ggml_argmax), its token embedding (get_rows from a device copy of the draft-vocabulary rows of
token_embd, 180 MiB for 64k Q4_K rows) and its h_nextn, and writes the KV of positions pos0..pos0+n-1.
Only the n token ids are read back. Every pass is the op sequence of a 1-token decode (same kernels,
same fusions), so the draft tokens are identical to the per-pass path.

- llama-ext: llama_set_mtp_draft_chain / llama_get_mtp_draft_tokens; cparams.mtp_draft_chain.
- qwen35 graph_mtp: the pass is a lambda shared by the normal and the chain graph; per pass the
  attention input points at row j of k_idxs / v_idxs / kq_mask, positions come from a per-token
  regrouped input (llm_graph_input_pos_chain). These inputs live on the device (the kv-cache input
  setters upload through a staging buffer when the tensor is not in host memory), otherwise the
  scheduler copies every row view as a separate split input (16 instead of 4 H2D copies).
- The chain graph keeps its own graph slot (gf_res_prev[1]), so it no longer alternates with the
  output-less catch-up graph in one slot.
- test-backend-ops: bit-exact GET_ROWS cases (f32/f16/q4_K, 5120 columns) - the device embedding
  must equal the host get_rows (q4_K: d*sc*q is exact in f32, so fma contraction cannot change it).

Per step, Qwen UD: draft phase (host timestamps around common_speculative_draft, median)
4.75 -> 3.94 ms at short context, 5.35 -> 4.43 ms at 25.5k; rocprofv3: 4 passes of 42 kernels with 5
input copies each -> one 104-kernel graph (3.63 ms wall, 3.22 ms busy) with 4 copies, step wall
38.45 -> 37.55 ms under the profiler.
Server spec_sweep (6 prompts x 3 seeds, T=1, ctx 204800, MTP n=4), interleaved A/B vs b1f8c19ac:
  Qwen UD:    36.39 / 36.42 -> 35.69 / 35.67 ms/step, 86.4 -> 88.0 t/s
  Uncensored: 34.57 / 34.56 -> 33.80 / 33.80 ms/step, 88.3 -> 90.4 t/s
Draft tokens identical to the per-pass path (dumps of 313 + 493 + 494 drafts, incl. a 25.5k-token
prompt, both models); tokens/step identical in the A/B; greedy MTP output byte-identical to b1f8c19ac.
