+// MTP draft chain (single NextN block with a reduced-vocabulary draft head, see llama_model_set_draft_head_vocab).
+// When enabled on an MTP context, a decode of a single-sequence batch of n <= LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_CHAIN_MAX consecutive
+// positions pos0..pos0+n-1 runs n chained greedy MTP passes in one graph: pass 0 reads the token and hidden state of
+// batch row 0, pass j > 0 the argmax token and h_nextn of pass j-1 (the other rows only provide the positions). The KV
+// of all n positions is written, no logits or embeddings are output; the n draft tokens are read with
+// llama_get_mtp_draft_tokens().
+// Returns false (and leaves it disabled) if the model does not support it.
+#define LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_CHAIN_MAX 16
+LLAMA_API bool llama_set_mtp_draft_chain(struct llama_context * ctx, bool enable);
+
+// The draft tokens of the last MTP draft chain decode (synchronizes), nullptr if there are none
